# Issue #45: retain a selected level's complete outline when a corner leaves
# the 3D viewport. GPU overlay scissoring clips it to the visible panel.
import ui/panels/bim_view_panel.dl

function require level outline {boolean:passed} named {a string:label}:
    execute:
        if passed = false:
            print ((the string form of "FAIL: ") + label) as a line
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 1)
        print ((the string form of "PASS: ") + label) as a line

function the blue level vertices of {bim canvas record:drawing}:
    execute:
        set count to 0
        loop cursor from 0 to the length of (drawing's batches's values):
            set batchValue to the item at cursor in (drawing's batches's values)
            if ((batchValue's red = 0) and (batchValue's green = 120)) and (batchValue's blue = 215):
                set count to count + (the length of (batchValue's pixels's values))
        return count

set editor to a new bim editor
set editor's documentValue's current to an empty bim model
set target to the address of (editor's documentValue's current)
set ground to add bim level named (the string form of "Ground") at 0.0 with height 3.0 to target
set editor's levelId to ground
set editor's selectionKind to bim level picked
set editor's selectionId to ground
set scene to an empty bim gpu scene
set scene's low to a cad vector3 with x -5.0, y -5.0 and z 0.0
set scene's high to a cad vector3 with x 20.0, y 5.0 and z 3.0
set layout to @intrinsic("construct", a bim screen layout record, 200.0, 200.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 200.0)
set camera to @intrinsic("construct", a bim camera record, (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0), 10.0, 0.0, 0.7, (the cad zero vector3), 10.0)

ignore set bim level extent of ground from (a cad vector2 with x -5.0 and y -5.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 5.0 and y 5.0) in target
set insideDrawing to a new bim canvas
draw bim levels of editor around scene in layout with camera on (the address of insideDrawing)
require level outline ((the blue level vertices of insideDrawing) = 72) named (the string form of "an inside outline has four edges and eight handles")

ignore set bim level extent of ground from (a cad vector2 with x -5.0 and y -5.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 20.0 and y 5.0) in target
set outsideCorner to the bim view point 20.0 5.0 0.0 in layout with camera
require level outline (outsideCorner's x > layout's width) named (the string form of "the dragged corner lies outside the viewport")
set crossingDrawing to a new bim canvas
draw bim levels of editor around scene in layout with camera on (the address of crossingDrawing)
require level outline ((the blue level vertices of crossingDrawing) = 72) named (the string form of "crossing edges remain recorded for viewport clipping")

set editor's selectionKind to bim nothing picked
set unselectedDrawing to a new bim canvas
draw bim levels of editor around scene in layout with camera on (the address of unselectedDrawing)
require level outline ((the blue level vertices of unselectedDrawing) = 0) named (the string form of "an unselected level has no blue selection outline")
